Tone_binary=1) in the second counterfactual dataset", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["counterfactual dataset 2"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 97, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[128, 128]], "assertion": "predicted the probability of a red card under each counterfactual", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["predicted probabilities"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 98, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[129, 129]], "assertion": "computed the adjusted risk difference as mean(P_dark) minus mean(P_light)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["adjusted risk difference computation"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 99, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[130, 131]], "note": "blank and 'Standard errors and confidence intervals:' label"}, {"id": 100, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[132, 132]], "assertion": "used a parametric bootstrap with 10,000 simulations for standard errors and CIs", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["bootstrap method"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 101, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[133, 133]], "assertion": "sampled parameter vectors from a multivariate normal distribution with mean=β̂ and covariance=Var(β̂)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["bootstrap parameter sampling"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 102, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[134, 134]], "assertion": "recomputed the risk difference for each simulated parameter vector", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["bootstrap recomputation"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 103, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[135, 135]], "assertion": "defined the 95% CI as the 2.5th and 97.5th percentiles of the simulated distribution", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["confidence interval method"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 104, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[136, 136]], "assertion": "computed the two-sided p-value as 2×min(P(RD≤0), P(RD≥0))", "polarity": "did", "targ